---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Dev"
  description="Web development and open-source work by Ryan Laird: Astro and TypeScript sites, structured content systems and automation, with live GitHub data."
>
  <div class="wrap page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="sl">Dev</p>
      <h1>Building accessible, data-driven web experiences.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        I design and develop Astro and React sites, shape structured content systems, and build clear digital
        experiences that are easy to use and maintain.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>What I do</h2>
      <div class="route-grid">
        <article class="route">
          <h3>Web development</h3>
          <p>Astro, React, TypeScript, content modelling, component systems and performance-aware front-end builds.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="route" data-tone="violet">
          <h3>Science communication</h3>
          <p>Space, climate and technical topics presented with structure, clarity and accessibility in mind.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="route" data-tone="amber">
          <h3>Automation</h3>
          <p>Scripts, APIs and workflows that reduce friction across publishing, research and digital asset management.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
  <h2>Featured areas</h2>
  <div class="route-grid">
    <article class="route">
      <h3>Open-source activity</h3>
      <p>
        A live view of the repositories, languages and recent contributions behind my work. It covers
        personal experiments, reusable components, documentation and practical tools for the web.
      </p>
      <a class="go" href="/dev/open-source/">Explore GitHub activity</a>
    </article>

    <article class="route" data-tone="violet">
      <h3>Productive digital systems</h3>
      <p>
        Development work in progress: websites, data models, publishing workflows and lightweight
        operational tools designed to help small teams organise knowledge and reduce repetitive work.
      </p>
      <a class="go" href="/dev/projects/">View development projects</a>
    </article>

    <article class="route" data-tone="amber">
      <h3>Open-source tools and experiments</h3>
      <p>
        A curated directory of software, datasets and prototypes I use, assess or build around. Each
        entry explains what it does, where it fits and how mature or production-ready it is.
      </p>
      <a class="go" href="/open-source/">Browse the open-source lab</a>
    </article>

    <article class="route" data-tone="sky">
      <h3>Space, climate and sustainability work</h3>
      <p>
        Selected projects combining strategic communication, digital platforms and technical research
        for organisations working in space, deep tech, sustainability and Earth observation.
      </p>
      <a class="go" href="/projects/">See selected projects</a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

  </div>
</Layout>
